Acceptance observations
-----------------------
1. screen_qr_exchange — passed
   Both real Android operators independently scanned the dynamic QR rendered
   on the physical robot screen. Matching map-management presence records were
   created only after the screen-render acknowledgement and exchange.

2. screen_short_code_exchange — passed
   With the Xiaomi rear camera physically covered, the operator selected the
   on-screen six-digit fallback, entered the value held only in observer
   memory, and confirmed it. Challenge map_challenge_7cb45e9e923d2e219930e110fe340e83
   was consumed at 2026-08-27T04:46:48.019544+00:00 and presence
   map_presence_3533b1ce2ff1363e5abb653856036e5e was established. The value
   itself was never printed, persisted, or included in this bundle.

3. screen_unavailable_fail_closed — passed
   The acknowledged screen boundary tests verified no registered screen,
   acknowledgement timeout, rejected presentation, and malformed challenge all
   fail closed. The real Gateway used the same loopback-only boundary.

4. mapping_authorization_one_shot — passed
   The authorization suite verified a mapping authorization is purpose-bound,
   short lived, consumed once, installation/actor/robot bound, and cannot be
   reused as teleoperation or map-management presence.

5. presence_expiry — passed
   The Gateway clock/HTTP integration suite verified the 15-minute upper bound
   and rejection after expiry without relying on client time.

6. presence_app_background — passed
   Real-device invalidation was observed repeatedly. The final fallback-created
   presence was invalidated at 2026-08-27T04:47:52.582813+00:00 with reason
   app_background and revision advanced from 1 to 2.

7. presence_token_revocation — passed
   Gateway integration tests verified paired-session/token revocation
   invalidates the bound presence and subsequent writes are rejected.

8. presence_lan_departure — passed
   Gateway integration tests verified a presence bound to robot-site-lan is
